  "details": "I am appreciative of the VRChat team for implementing the avatar content filters to allow one to further tailor their experience to be more comfortable and wholesome, but due to these filters, I've been having a conundrum.\n\nFriends who have their avatars tagged with the corresponding filter enabled will show up as a grey robot. I don't know about the rest of you, but I prioritize seeing my friends' avatars and expressions in order to properly communicate with them. One of two things needs to happen; either I disable my filters or ask them to change avatars, and most people don't like being told what to do no matter how politely you ask.\n\nSo I propose there be a toggle for friends' avatars to bypass the filters, just like with Safety Settings. I feel like it makes even more sense here since even choosing to manually 'show' a friend's avatar doesn't bypass it and they're still stuck as a grey robot from your perspective.\n\nTL;DR: Friends override toggle for content filters, please.",
